          "What if you do NOT need per-room schedules, only peak instantaneous concurrency or active interval windows across 100,000 bursts? The Sweep-Line paradigm flattens every `[start, end)` interval into two tiny independent boundary deltas: `(start, +1)` and `(end, -1)`.",
          "Sort all `2N` events chronologically and walk a single `running_active` counter left-to-right! Whenever `running_active` climbs above previous bests, record peak concurrency cleanly in `O(N log N)` time and minimal flat tuple storage.",
