          "William Pugh invented an astonishingly elegant lock-friendly alternative in 1989: the **Skip List**! Start with a normal sorted singly linked list at **Level 0** (`1 -> 3 -> 7 -> 12 -> 19 -> ...`), then stack sparse express-lane pointers cleanly above selected nodes at Levels `1, 2, 3, ...`!",
