          "Hart, Nilsson, and Raphael (1968) fused BOTH signals cleanly into **A* Search**: `f(n) = g(n) + h(n)`, where `g(n)` = exact verified shortest cost from Start to `n`, and `h(n)` = heuristic estimate of remaining cost from `n` to Goal `G`!",
