          "First, given candidate proprietary trade baskets `(trade_id, risk_cost, expected_alpha_bps)` competing inside a strict `max_risk` ceiling, our Branch-and-Bound optimizer sorts trades descending by alpha-per-unit-risk, computes fractional optimistic relaxation upper bounds, and expands leading states cleanly via Max-Heap while logging exact pruned vs explored nodes!",
          "Second, routing urgent execution packets across a regional datacenter fiber mesh modeled as a 2D switch topology grid uses tie-broken A* (`(g + h, -g, r, c)`) with consistent Manhattan lower-bound estimates (`h <= h*`). Comparing `nodes_expanded` side-by-side against Dijkstra (`h = 0`) confirms exact shortest latency equivalence with dramatic expansion reduction!",
          "Notice that keeping consistent priority tuple schemas `(prio_tuple, g, r, c)` across BOTH Dijkstra and A* eliminates Python mixed-type heap crashes cleanly!",
